Section: 2.1 ARCHITECTURE
Text: 2.1 ARCHITECTURE During training, the input to our ConvNets is a ﬁxed-size 224 × 224 RGB image. The only pre- processing we do is subtracting the mean RGB value, computed on the training set, from each pixel. The image is passed through a stack of convolutional (conv.) layers, where we use ﬁlters with a very small receptive ﬁeld: 3 × 3 (which is the smallest size to capture the notion of left/right, up/down, center).

